	Two similar suggestions:                         

	#1) Let polymorph wands transmute wands of a given type into 
traps of the given type; this adds the feature of creating traps, and
deals with the biggest problem of polypiling, while still allowing 
people with patience or need to transform piles of armor and weapons
and so forth into better versions.
	#2) Let polymorph wands have a chance to convert the floor into,
say, fountains, sinks, traps, and other ground characters.  This has the
effect of making polypiling significantly more difficult over time, as 
rings disappear into sinks and teleport traps scatter your piles over 
the dungeon, without actually ruling it out.

	Obviously, only one of these should be implemented; either of 
them allows one to create traps with some trying, and puts a "sensible"
limitation on polymorphing wands into wishes.

